What It Is

This tree is not older than the forest.
It is newer than everything else.

It exists where the forest has learned how to stop, briefly, without dying.

The white leaves are not bleached or dead. They are complete. Each leaf is identical in shape, weight, and spacing, as if grown from a single decision repeated flawlessly. No insects touch them. No moss dares the bark. Roots exist, but do not surface.

The forest has agreed, for now, not to interfere.
Read-Aloud: Arrival

    The forest thins without opening.
    One tree stands alone, its pale leaves bright without reflecting light.

    The air beneath it is cool and still, as if the world has paused mid-breath.

    Sound dulls here. Not silence. Precision.

    You realize nothing at its base has ever been allowed to begin.

Pause. Let them step or not step.
The Nature of the Stillness

Inside the tree’s shade:

    Wind does not enter

    Leaves do not fall

    Magic aligns cleanly

    Cause and effect feel immediate and trustworthy

This is not safety.
This is determinism.

The forest is not watching this space closely because nothing unexpected happens here.
What the Tree Allows

While within the shade:

    Actions resolve cleanly

    Tools behave exactly as intended

    Spells feel crisp, exact, and restrained

    Plans work if they were sound to begin with

There is no luck here.
There is no forgiveness either.

Mistakes land precisely.
