How the Forest Treats This Place

The forest does not protect the tree.

It routes around it.

Paths bend slightly away. Roots hesitate at the perimeter. Predators avoid crossing the shade, not out of fear, but because nothing interesting happens there.

This is a place the forest uses when it needs to remember what “exactly one thing” feels like.
Player-Facing Tells

